00:29:54.880 --> 00:29:58.680
about. Obviously Capcom was the developer on the arcade versions of all these.

00:29:58.840 --> 00:30:03.100
Yeah. But apparently this is their first go at the NES version, uh, of anything.

00:30:03.100 --> 00:30:08.200
So that's a big, uh, step for 1987 in general is just that like, you know, a major third

00:30:08.200 --> 00:30:10.640
party company is learning to actually use the hardware.

00:30:11.060 --> 00:30:15.280
And sure enough, we're going to see a bunch of big games from Capcom on the system.

00:30:15.420 --> 00:30:17.840
So it's good that they're, uh, they're working on it.

00:30:18.600 --> 00:30:20.120
It's good that they're learning now.

00:30:20.120 --> 00:30:24.400
So, so I think like with that in mind, you know, like there's not that many kinks.

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:26.960
So I think that's like really, that says something for Capcom's quality.

00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:32.140
Yeah, no, I never, I never, like a lot of the games we played like that are third party

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:38.860
so far have been, have actually had technical issues like slow down and, and, uh, sprite

00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:42.140
flicker or actual sprite, uh, loss.

00:30:42.140 --> 00:30:48.340
And it's, it's good to see, um, the third party kind of get it together already.

00:30:48.620 --> 00:30:52.180
